        <li><a href="/guides/houlton-dispensary-guide">Houlton Dispensary Guide</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/calais-dispensary-guide">Calais Dispensary Guide</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/maine-cannabis-opt-in-tracker">Maine Cannabis Opt-In Tracker</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/maine-cannabis-market">Maine Cannabis Market</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="faq-section">
    <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <Faq
      questions={[
        { q: "Are there cannabis dispensaries in Presque Isle, Maine?", a: "Yes. Presque Isle has two dispensaries on Main Street: Full Bloom Cannabis (483 Main St) and Royal Leaf Apothecary (415 Main St). Richardson Remedies in Caribou (9 Bog Rd) is a 10-minute drive south and serves the broader Aroostook region." },
        { q: "What is the closest dispensary to Presque Isle?", a: "In town: Full Bloom Cannabis (483 Main St) and Royal Leaf Apothecary (415 Main St). Within 15 minutes in Caribou: Richardson Remedies (9 Bog Rd)." },
        { q: "Does Presque Isle allow recreational cannabis?", a: "Yes. The city permits adult-use retail, but in March 2026 the council approved a temporary moratorium on new marijuana business licenses to review local regulations." },
        { q: "What is Presque Isle Maine known for?", a: "Presque Isle is the largest city in Aroostook County — the largest county east of the Mississippi, with ~67,000 residents across 6,672 sq mi. It is home to UMaine Presque Isle and serves as the commercial and healthcare hub of northern Aroostook." },
      ]}
    />
  </section>

  <p class="disclaimer"><strong>Disclaimer:</strong> Information is provided for general reference only. Dispensary hours, product availability, and policies can change. Always verify details directly with the dispensary before planning a visit.</p>
</article>
